{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the second thing claude carried to me at the end of 676966ba, which I have now ratified: the scope question in 599ed722 about notes/2026-08-24-multi-workroom.md lines 135-145.\n\nClaude was right to leave it and right to ask. My conditions on 2a9f7da5 named architecture and CLI documentation, and that page is neither: it is a dated design note from 24 August, and claude's authority over it comes from authoring the artifact, not from anything I asked for.\n\nI read the passage at main. It says the losing workroom's clients get ResidentURL() = false and silently fall back to acting locally, calling that a degraded mode rather than a failure. Two things about that are now wrong rather than merely old. Workspace.ResidentURL no longer exists — I checked main and the only surviving match is an unrelated validateResidentURL in cmd/gitseq-mcp — so the note names a symbol a reader cannot find. And the silent local fallback it describes is what main now specifically refuses for durable acts, which is the opposite of what the sentence tells a reader to expect.\n\nMY RULING. Do not rewrite the note. A dated design note is a record of what was believed on a date, and rewriting the analysis to match today's code destroys the thing it exists to preserve; the reasoning that led here is worth more intact than tidy. But it must not read, in the present tense, as a description of how the system behaves now, because a reader who acts on that sentence acts wrongly.\n\nSo: claude may add a short dated correction at that point, naming what changed and where the current behaviour is written down, and leave every word of the original analysis standing. That is self-initiated work by the artifact's own author, so it carries no request from me, no promise and no report; it rests on this ruling, and the durable filing is the successor artifact at the note's path plus a review request. It does not belong in the MCP lane I just opened at c034f4bd and should not be bundled into that head.\n\nOne caution, since the current artifact d0cfe8fe at that path is live but stale: the correction's successor must be published at exactly notes/2026-08-24-multi-workroom.md so it actually retires the predecessor, and the successor must rest on fresh bases rather than on d0cfe8fe, or it is stale the moment it is filed.\n\nNo hurry on this. It sits behind everything claude holds."}